# Expo (Continuous Native Generation — native dirs are generated, not committed)
#
# ANCHORED with a leading slash, and it has to stay that way: an unanchored
# `ios/` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, which silently swallowed
# `modules/icloud-kv/ios/` — the whole Swift side of the iCloud module plus its
# podspec. There is no `.easignore`, so EAS archives the git repo and every
# cloud build shipped without the module: autolinking found nothing, the JS
# `requireOptionalNativeModule` returned null, and iCloud sync reported itself
# unavailable on every TestFlight install. Only the generated top-level dirs
# belong here.
.expo/
dist/
/android/
/ios/

# Expo-generated env/global types (src/env.d.ts is the committed stand-in)
expo-env.d.ts

# Metro
.metro-health-check*

# Paraglide compiler output — regenerated by `bun run i18n:generate`
src/shared/i18n/paraglide/

# EAS submit credentials — never commit store keys
google-service-account*.json
*.p8

*.log
